en-US.translator.usage:
**What it does**: turns foreign-language material into searchable, question-generatable Chinese knowledge assets (positioning: sinicize material + make translations assets).

**How to use**:
1. Translate as you chat: tell Baize "Translate this passage into Chinese" (or copy text in any app and trigger the selection shortcut, then add "translate"; shortcut defaults and effective keys are in "Settings → Shortcuts") — translation only, term protection, format fidelity;
2. Document translation: tell Baize "Translate <document name>" — the cache is checked automatically (instant when the source document is unchanged); on a miss it translates batch by batch with source material and writes results to sys-hub "Translation/<source repo>/"; the translation header links back to the source document, and once in the library it's searchable and question-generatable;
3. Default auto direction (Chinese source → English, otherwise → Chinese); you can also specify "translate into Japanese".

**Notes**: translation is done by your current Agent model (consumes model quota; long documents take multiple batches); no translation-service keys to configure.

